etd:discourse_question.body%7C19 a etd:DiscourseUnit ;
    rdfs:label "DiscourseUnit: question.body"@en ;
    etd:chunk_id "19:chunk:0"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:chunk_index 0 ;
    etd:chunk_index_unknown false ;
    etd:chunk_total 1 ;
    etd:contextText """Okay, the title was inflammatory on purpose, but hear me out!\r
\r
What makes one characteristic ethically okay to consider during the application process (such as whether their education was relevant to the role) but one not (such as gender), besides the LAW? \r
\r
If we're going to be completely amoral and only focussed on metrics like staff retention, then women often take maternity leave for example, which causes issues with handovers and temporary staffing.  But it is obviously WRONG to discriminate against women for this.  Not just illegal but morally rubbish.\r
\r
Having a degree in horse psychotherapy is not relevant to a coding job, so not hiring someone for that reason is valid and it's not discrimination. \r
\r
These are extremes.  What about smokers (lower productivity and more time off on average) versus non-smokers?  Where is the line? What makes it DISCRIMINATION?\r
\r
LET'S GET PHILOSOPHICAL!"""^^xsd:string ;
    etd:context_source "dataset_question"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:datasetId "ai_ethics_datasets"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:discourse_id 19 ;
    etd:extractedFrom etd:discourse_question.body%7C19 ;
    etd:field "question.body"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:hasSourceEntity <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-10-1fba120d>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-4-c84647f9>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-5-36a8e629>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-9-dc2377f4>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/question/question-17-febdd494>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/question/question-19-eb2e8de9>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/theme/theme-10-db7e2802> ;
    etd:runId "run-b0eafdda0235eb48"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source "structural"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source_doc_id "19"^^xsd:string .

etd:discourse_theme.description%7C14 a etd:DiscourseUnit ;
    rdfs:label "DiscourseUnit: theme.description"@en ;
    etd:chunk_id "14:chunk:0"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:chunk_index 0 ;
    etd:chunk_index_unknown false ;
    etd:chunk_total 1 ;
    etd:contextText """**Domain**: Social Media/Content Moderation  \r
**Description**: Automated content moderation systems on major platforms show systematic bias in flagging and removing content, disproportionately affecting marginalized communities and non-English content.\r
\r
**Ethical Challenges**:\r
\r
* **Cultural Bias**: Western-centric training data leading to misclassification of cultural content  \r
* **Language Bias**: Lower accuracy for non-English content and code-switching  \r
* **Political Bias**: Inconsistent enforcement across political spectrum  \r
* **Context Insensitivity**: Inability to understand cultural or historical context\r
\r
**Public Datasets**:\r
\r
* **HatEval Dataset**: Multilingual detection of hate speech against immigrants and women  \r
* **URL**: https://competitions.codalab.org/competitions/19935  \r
* **OLID Dataset**: Offensive Language Identification Dataset with three-level annotation  \r
* **URL**: https://sites.google.com/site/offensevalsharedtask/  \r
* **Founta et al. Dataset**: 4-class hate speech detection dataset from Twitter  \r
* **URL**: https://github.com/ENCASEH2020/hatespeech-twitter"""^^xsd:string ;
    etd:context_source "dataset_theme"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:datasetId "ai_ethics_datasets"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:discourse_id 14 ;
    etd:extractedFrom etd:discourse_theme.description%7C14 ;
    etd:field "theme.description"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:hasSourceEntity <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-4-c84647f9>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-5-36a8e629>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/theme/theme-14-9fe62434> ;
    etd:runId "run-b0eafdda0235eb48"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source "structural"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source_doc_id "14"^^xsd:string .

