etd:discourse_theme.description%7C10 a etd:DiscourseUnit ;
    rdfs:label "DiscourseUnit: theme.description"@en ;
    etd:chunk_id "10:chunk:0"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:chunk_index 0 ;
    etd:chunk_index_unknown false ;
    etd:chunk_total 1 ;
    etd:contextText """**Domain**: Human Resources/Employment  \r
**Description**: Amazon developed an AI recruitment tool (2014-2017) that systematically discriminated against women, leading to its termination. Recent University of Washington studies (2024) found similar bias in LLMs for resume screening.\r
\r
**Ethical Challenges**:\r
\r
* **Gender Bias**: Amazon's system penalized resumes containing words like "women's" and downgraded graduates from women's colleges  \r
* **Intersectional Bias**: UW study found names associated with Black women were never favored over white men  \r
* **Historical Inequality Perpetuation**: AI trained on historical workforce data predominantly male  \r
* **Disparate Impact Discrimination**: Under Title VII violations\r
\r
**Public Datasets**:\r
\r
* **Primary**: Adult/Census Income Dataset \\- UCI Machine Learning Repository  \r
* **URL**: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/20/census+income  \r
* **MIT Case Study**: https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/res-ec-001-exploring-fairness-in-machine-learning-for-international-development-spring-2020/pages/module-four-case-studies/case-study-mitigating-gender-bias/  \r
* **Content**: 48,842 records of census data for predicting income \\>$50K/year with 13 features  \r
* **Bias Use**: Widely used for studying bias in income prediction across demographic groups  \r
* **Additional Platforms**: Available on fairness toolkits \\- https://fairmlbook.org/datasets.html"""^^xsd:string ;
    etd:context_source "dataset_theme"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:datasetId "ai_ethics_datasets"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:discourse_id 10 ;
    etd:extractedFrom etd:discourse_theme.description%7C10 ;
    etd:field "theme.description"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:hasSourceEntity <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-4-c84647f9>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-5-36a8e629>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/theme/theme-10-db7e2802> ;
    etd:runId "run-b0eafdda0235eb48"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source "structural"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source_doc_id "10"^^xsd:string .

etd:discourse_theme.description%7C7 a etd:DiscourseUnit ;
    rdfs:label "DiscourseUnit: theme.description"@en ;
    etd:chunk_id "7:chunk:0"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:chunk_index 0 ;
    etd:chunk_index_unknown false ;
    etd:chunk_total 1 ;
    etd:contextText """**Domain**: Healthcare/Medical AI  \r
**Description**: Obermeyer et al. (2019) study in Science revealed racial bias in commercial health risk algorithms affecting \\~200 million Americans annually, used to identify patients needing additional care programs.\r
\r
**Ethical Challenges**:\r
\r
* **Measurement Bias**: Algorithm used healthcare spending as proxy for health needs, but Black patients spent \\~$1,800 less annually than white patients with identical conditions  \r
* **Disparate Impact**: Black patients were 2.6 times less likely to receive additional care despite greater medical need  \r
* **Scale of Impact**: Affects millions of healthcare decisions  \r
* **Proxy Problem**: Seemingly neutral metrics can incorporate systemic bias\r
\r
**Public Datasets**:\r
\r
* **Primary**: MIMIC-CXR Database (PhysioNet)  \r
* **URL**: https://physionet.org/content/mimic-cxr/2.0.0/  \r
* **Content**: 377,110 chest X-ray images from Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center  \r
* **Bias Documentation**: Documented bias in medical image classifiers by race, sex, age, and insurance type  \r
* **Access**: Requires credentials but publicly available for research"""^^xsd:string ;
    etd:context_source "dataset_theme"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:datasetId "ai_ethics_datasets"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:discourse_id 7 ;
    etd:extractedFrom etd:discourse_theme.description%7C7 ;
    etd:field "theme.description"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:hasSourceEntity <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-4-c84647f9>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-5-36a8e629>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/theme/theme-7-d2d078c8> ;
    etd:runId "run-b0eafdda0235eb48"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source "structural"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source_doc_id "7"^^xsd:string .

