etd:discourse_answer.description%7C23 a etd:DiscourseUnit ;
    rdfs:label "DiscourseUnit: answer.description"@en ;
    etd:chunk_id "23:chunk:0"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:chunk_index 0 ;
    etd:chunk_index_unknown false ;
    etd:chunk_total 1 ;
    etd:contextText """I would echo Holly & Adrian - really good points. Might I also suggest:\r
\r
Algorithms can perpetuate or even amplify existing biases if they are trained on biased historical data (e.g., past job match/hiring decisions that favored certain genders, ethnicities, or age groups). Such bias can occur even if the relevant data on the CV is obfuscated from the model because other elements may 'proxy' this information. This is one of the major challenges to solve for a fair job matching AI.\r
\r
Additionally, CVs/Resumes usually contain at least some sensitive personal data. Improper handling can lead to data breaches or misuse. This must be mitigated somehow. Somewhat related is that we don't really know how ChatGPT will look to monetise, and for now OpenAI are being forced to retain ALL chatlogs due to a court decision (even before they would retain this unless you opted out) so who knows what may happen to this data if for example an organisation uses the OpenAI API for this process."""^^xsd:string ;
    etd:context_source "dataset_answer"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:datasetId "ai_ethics_datasets"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:discourse_id 23 ;
    etd:extractedFrom etd:discourse_answer.description%7C23 ;
    etd:field "answer.description"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:hasSourceEntity <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/answer/answer-23-458318a2>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-35-7aee2084>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-36-33b967cd>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-4-c84647f9>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-47-dbc100d9>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/person/expert-5-36a8e629>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/question/question-16-a1cc6531>,
        <https://alfie-project.eu/etd-hub/entity/theme/theme-10-db7e2802> ;
    etd:runId "run-b0eafdda0235eb48"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source "structural"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:source_doc_id "23"^^xsd:string .

etd:discourse_theme.description%7C11 a etd:DiscourseUnit ;
    rdfs:label "DiscourseUnit: theme.description"@en ;
    etd:chunk_id "11:chunk:0"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:chunk_index 0 ;
    etd:chunk_index_unknown false ;
    etd:chunk_total 1 ;
    etd:contextText """**Domain**: Education/Assessment  \r
**Description**: Automated Essay Scoring (AES) systems show systematic bias against students from marginalized groups. 2024 studies found GPT-4o incorrectly predicted academic failure for Black students 19% of the time vs. 12% for white students.\r
\r
**Ethical Challenges**:\r
\r
* **Linguistic Bias**: Against non-native English speakers and dialectal variations  \r
* **Cultural Bias**: Preference for mainstream cultural references and writing conventions  \r
* **Socioeconomic Bias**: Correlated with writing style differences across economic classes  \r
* **Educational Gap Perpetuation**: Biased algorithms can reinforce existing educational disparities\r
\r
**Public Datasets**:\r
\r
* **Primary**: ASAP (Automated Student Assessment Prize) Dataset  \r
* **URL**: https://www.kaggle.com/c/asap-aes/data  \r
* **Papers with Code**: https://paperswithcode.com/dataset/asap  \r
* **Source**: Kaggle Competition Data  \r
* **Content**: \\~12,800 essays from grades 7-10 across 8 different prompts  \r
* **Enhanced**: ASAP 2.0 Dataset (2024) \\- 24,000 argumentative essays with explicit bias considerations  \r
* **ASAP 2.0 URL**: https://the-learning-agency-lab.com/learning-exchange/asap-2-0-dataset/  \r
* **GitHub Implementation**: https://github.com/Turanga1/Automated-Essay-Scoring"""^^xsd:string ;
    etd:context_source "dataset_theme"^^xsd:string ;
    etd:datasetId "ai_ethics_datasets"^^xsd:string ;
